body:json {
  {
    "content": "title: ExpressJS Explorer: Your Node.js Web Dev Journey!\ndescription: Embark on an exciting adventure into the world of ExpressJS! Master the core fundamentals of this powerful Node.js web framework with our interactive quiz app. Test your knowledge on routing, middleware, templating, and more through engaging quizzes and challenges. Track your progress, unlock achievements, and level up your ExpressJS skills. Whether you're a beginner taking your first steps or an experienced developer sharpening your axe, ExpressJS Explorer provides a fun, intuitive, and rewarding learning experience. Get ready to build robust and scalable web applications – Download now and start exploring!\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: Which HTTP method is typically used to retrieve data from a server?\noptions:\n1. POST\n2. PUT\n3. GET [correct]\n4. DELETE\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs, HTTP\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion: Middleware functions in ExpressJS always have access to the request and response objects.\ncorrect: true\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs, Middleware\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Explain the purpose of `app.use()` in ExpressJS.\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs, Middleware\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: Which of the following are commonly used template engines with ExpressJS?\noptions:\n1. Pug [correct]\n2. Handlebars [correct]\n3. Django\n4. Spring\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs, Templating\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: What does REST stand for in the context of web services?\noptions:\n1. Really Efficient System Technology\n2. Representational State Transfer [correct]\n3. Reliable Error System Troubleshooting\n4. Rapid Execution System Toolkit\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs, REST\n\n---question---\ntype: trueFalse\nquestion:  ExpressJS is built on top of the Node.js `http` module.\ncorrect: true\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Describe the difference between `req.params` and `req.query` in ExpressJS.\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs, Routing, HTTP\n\n---question---\ntype: multiSelect\nquestion: Which of the following are common tasks for middleware in ExpressJS?\noptions:\n1. Logging requests [correct]\n2. Parsing request bodies [correct]\n3.  Handling database connections\n4.  Rendering templates\ntags: Expressjs, Nodejs, Middleware\n"
  }
}
